@startuml j3-booking-and-call-back
!include style.iuml
title J3 Booking request and call-back
actor Patient
participant "Chat page\n(index.html, chat.js)" as Chat
participant "core.js" as Core
database "localStorage" as LS
participant "WhatsApp" as WA
autonumber

Patient -> Chat : "I want to book a check-up tomorrow at 5 pm"
Chat -> Core : FD.answer(q, data)
Core -> Core : bookingWhen(t): day (today, tomorrow, a weekday or "12 Nov")\nand time ("5:00 pm", morning, afternoon, evening)
note right of Core
Booking needs a booking word, not a how-to-book,
cancel or walk-in question, and a time or a wish
("I want", "please", "need"). Emergency, discount
and medical are checked first.
end note
Core --> Chat : kind "booking", status "needs human",\nT[lang].booking(data, when) + bookingDayNote(): that day's hours\nwhen one weekday is named; bookingTime (or "not given"), bookingDate
note over Chat : no model call for a booking
Chat -> Core : FD.openNow(data)
alt the clinic is closed now
  Chat -> Core : FD.nextOpening(data)
  Core --> Chat : "today at 9:00 am", "tomorrow at ..." or "<Day> at ..."
  Chat -> Chat : afterHoursNote = UI[lang].closedNote(next)
end
Chat -> Core : FD.addTicket({... kind "booking", bookingTime, afterHours, callBack: true})
Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets
Chat --> Patient : reply "passed your request for <time> ... call you back within 2 working hours",\n"Continue on WhatsApp", after-hours note when closed, call-back form
note right of Chat : the note and the form sit beside the .bot-msg, never inside it
Chat --> Patient : v1.7.2, callback-ask.js: while no number is saved, a line at the top of the form:\n"We do not have a phone number for you yet ...", or call the clinic on its own number\n(English, Hindi, Telugu); gone once a number is saved

opt Patient leaves a name and phone
  Patient -> Chat : name (optional), country code and phone, presses Save
  Chat -> Chat : intlNumber(code, phone): length checked for that country,\na leading 0 dropped, result +<code><number>
  alt the number does not fit the country
    Chat --> Patient : "Check the number for the country you chose ..."
  else it fits
    Chat -> Core : FD.updateTicket(id, {contactName, contactPhone})
    Core -> LS : write frontdesk.tickets
    Chat --> Patient : form replaced by "Thank you, <name>. We will call <phone>."
  end
end
opt Patient taps Continue on WhatsApp
  Patient -> WA : wa.me/91<whatsapp digits>?text=<the request>
end
note over Chat, LS : on /staff the ticket shows "requested <time>", "after hours" and sits in the call list (J4)
@enduml
